+## API keys and audit (schema 3)
+
+- `apiKeys` contains `{ key, name, role }` records. Roles are `viewer`, `cook`,
+  and `manager`. Schema 2 files migrate with empty keys (access denied until
+  keys are configured) and an empty audit log; existing collections are preserved.
+- `audit` is append-only: `{ time, name, method, path, status }`. `time` is an
+  ISO instant and `name` is the API key name, never the secret key.
+- Successful HTTP requests that save data append an audit entry in the same
+  save as the data change. Reads and rejected requests do not append entries.
